 "name": "card-looks",
 "description": "Film looks loaded from the SD card and kept in the camera. A look file C:\\EPM2LOOK.BIN (docs/reference/look-file-format.md) holds up to 12 looks, one per art-filter menu entry. At the first menu or playback screen of a session, when the card is not being written, the dormant task USRTEST_A reads the file into the EEROM settings bank's unused tail (0x603FD040), checks it (magic, version, lengths, CRC-32, camera and firmware, slots and kinds), copies it into the store at 0x603F8000 and, when a byte changed, calls the bank save API 0x7E680272. At every start (the first GUI state) and after a load the task checks the store and writes its looks into the slots' tables (both aliases): saturation pair, six-axis values, art matrix, chroma record, and each tone table made from the look's curve and the stock default table, as the film generator does; the black-and-white slot (Grainy Film) takes its matrix and two tables. Then the look stages recompute (the boot init's refresh stores). A bad file changes nothing; without a file the stored looks stay. A hook on the GUI state setter's trace call 0x7ECDF6E4 starts the task (the site and task of the camera-tested debug log, which this build does not have), code in free runs of segment 2, the slot table in two data areas of segment 3. A delta on data/builds/films-12d.json: every expect is a byte string of that build. See experiments/2026-11-17-card-looks/design.md section 9.3.",
